// TEST: Leading Minus At Statement Column (rejects)
// ERROR: BL1001 @ 12:1
// ERROR-CONTAINS: indented past the start of that statement
// A line that opens with a binary operator continues the expression above
// only when it is indented past the start of that statement (formalism
// §15.1). At the statement's own column it is ambiguous -- `let y = x` then
// `- 3` used to be two statements: y = 5 and a printed bare -3, silently --
// so it is refused. Indent it to subtract (see basic/064), or write `(-3)`
// for a new statement.
let x = 5
let y = x
- 3
